cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, build on one of its measurements, or take one of
  its pieces, please cite it. Every figure the project publishes is in
  docs/etappes/ with its limits; cite the etappe for the figure.
type: software
title: >-
  Theogony: an open vector-graph knowledge substrate beneath AI, queried by
  Spreading Activation
authors:
  - family-names: Reinehr
    given-names: Jakob
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-04-16"
repository-code: https://github.com/theogony-project/theogony
url: https://github.com/theogony-project/theogony
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - knowledge substrate
  - knowledge graph
  - spreading activation
  - retrieval
  - graph RAG
  - language model memory
  - model context protocol
  - provenance
  - contradiction
  - open commons
abstract: >-
  Theogony builds a knowledge layer beneath AI systems as an open commons:
  knowledge kept as vectors and typed, weighted edges in a LanceDB and PyTorch
  mesh that a model activates by Spreading Activation instead of reading text,
  with provenance, time and contradiction as first-class fields. The
  repository ships the substrate, a reader (Kadmos) that turns text into mesh,
  a maintenance tick with decay that spares what fired, an MCP server with no
  language model on the retrieval path, and the complete measurement record,
  negative results included. On 1,000 questions of 2WikiMultihopQA the edges
  of the mesh were worth 3.6 points of exact match over the same entities
  without them.
